  "description": "Potential users of online psychological therapy make seven quick visual choices: preferred therapist sex; preferred colour (nine counselling-room colours); one of three video-call backgrounds rising in complexity and naturalness; dressed-up vs casual female and male therapist figures; and high vs low naturalness and high vs low complexity decoration. The time to each choice is recorded. Rebuilt from Lobato Rincón, Medina Sánchez & Tovar Bordón (2025), Vision 9(2): 43, with the paper's Figure 1–3 images and Table 1 colours (CC BY 4.0). Analysis as in the paper: choice shares by age group, gender, education and therapy experience (chi-square), response times by option (ANOVA, responses under 20 s), decision trees / logistic regression for each choice.",
